#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read from the request. Deliberately NOT DMN-backed: the four branches are not computable from a fact anyone reports — they are what was asked for, and a table that pretended otherwise would return an answer that is not the request."
msgstr ""

#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:189
#. Diagram label
msgid "retire"
msgstr ""

#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:137
#. Diagram label
msgid "Retire an actor — never delete one"
msgstr ""

#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:86
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs only after CallActivity_CodeChangeReview has already completed its own review, because the breakage this lane exists to catch — a join across role, lane, actor and skill — is invisible to a code reviewer reading the diff in isolation; ordinary code review clears the edit, and only this lane's whole-graph pass can tell whether it silently broke something three diagrams away."
msgstr ""

#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:175
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The administrator's call, not the pipeline's: `kg:audit:check` fails on `critical` and `kg:audit:strict` adds `major`, so what holds a change is a policy choice about this instance rather than arithmetic the audit performs."
msgstr ""

#: processes/actor-role-administration.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The join every other diagram depends on. An empty `roles` is a DETERMINED empty — it says the actor takes on none — and is not the same as an absent one, which asserts nothing."
msgstr ""

